      <h1>Meetily Review: The Best Local AI Meeting Assistant in 2026?</h1>
      <p class="lede">Meetily is a Rust-based, privacy-first AI meeting assistant that runs 100% locally. We tested its live transcription, summarization, and how it stacks up against Otter and Fireflies.</p>
      <div class="article-meta">
        <div class="meta-item"><i class="far fa-calendar"></i> <span>2026-07-12</span></div>
        <div class="meta-item"><i class="far fa-clock"></i> <span>9 min read</span></div>
        <div class="meta-item"><i class="far fa-user"></i> <span>AI Tool Hub Editorial</span></div>
        <div class="meta-item reviewer"><i class="fas fa-user-check"></i> <span>Reviewed by <strong>Lin Chen</strong>, Lead Reviewer (5+ years testing AI tools)</span></div>
      </div>
    </header>
      <img src="/images/blog/meetily-review-best-local-ai-meeting-assistant-2026/hero.webp" onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='/images/blog/meetily-review-best-local-ai-meeting-assistant-2026/hero.jpg'" alt="Meetily Review: The Best Local AI Meeting Assistant in 2026?" style="width:100%;border-radius:12px;margin:24px 0;" loading="eager" />

    <section class="blog-content">
<p>If you have hesitated to invite Otter or Fireflies into a sensitive sales call, investor update, or therapy appointment because you do not know where the recording ends up, you are not alone. Meetily, a new Rust-based open-source AI meeting assistant that transcribes and summarizes conversations entirely on your own machine, is quickly climbing GitHub’s trending charts as the privacy-first alternative everyone has been waiting for.</p>

